    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i'll check the container logs again. but honestly it feels so random. like it's almost like something is messing with it on purpose. is there any way to actually isolate the environment to be 100% sure it's not just some weird ghost in the system or something?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If you suspect some unseen interference, the best way to isolate it is to make the environment as predictable as possible. You could try running the exact same test suite locally on your machine, ensuring your local environment perfectly mirrors the Jenkins agent setup, perhaps even using the same Docker image version. If it passes locally but fails in Jenkins, you've confirmed the environment is the culprit, and you can then focus your investigation on the pipeline configuration or agent setup. This process of rigorous replication is key to defeating the \"ghost in the system.\"",
      "source": "target",
